Subject: [PATCH] 5182: the plan wall refuses a plan only when the ask it
 points to will go
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Giorgi (thread 52292): „ჯობია თორნიკეს დავუკავშირდეთ…". The plan wall
refused his new plan as „your own instruction is the permission", because the
line named SOME contact of his (messageNamesOwnContact); the ask wall refused
the ask to Tornike, because the line did not name THIS contact by his own
label. Neither door opened, the model asked for a yes in text, his
„ვადასტურებ" approved the old plan, and nothing was sent. For the one person a
plan adds, the plan wall now asks the ask wall's own question
(ownerLineNamesThisContact), so a refused plan always means an ask that goes,
and otherwise the plan is proposed and one approval starts it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
